  "description": "Discontinued. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic Rocket.\n\nThe Cotic Rocket Gen4 was our rough and tough, race proven steel full suspension enduro bike for 27.5\" wheels. 165mm rear travel, up to a 170mm fork. See the Rocket archive for the other generations.\n\nThe Rocket is wild and fast and just so much fun, designed to get you down the rowdiest trails with an infectious grin on your face. 165mm of trail eating travel and the subtly supple Reynolds 853 steel frame gives you ground moulding traction in the corners, and keeps you trucking through the chunkiest rock gardens and most sketchy chutes you can find. droplink still lets you skip and pop down the trail, seeking out gaps and jumps, and lets you scramble back to the top like a mountain goat.\n\nOur signature Longshot geometry, with its slack head angle, short stem and low standover, gets a steeper seat angle and longer reach over the previous model for improved climbing, keeping your weight central over the bike. It balances quick handling from the nimble 27.5\" wheels with a swaggering \"bring it on\" attitude that needs no encouragement to go blisteringly fast. Developed on tough Peak District trails, the Rocket was ready for anything you could throw at it.",
